From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:38:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build: make the macOS deployment target and Linux glibc
 target configurable

Electrobun hard-codes macOS 14.0 for every Mach-O and links Linux binaries
against the build host's glibc (Ubuntu 24.04, glibc 2.39). Apps that support
macOS 13 or Ubuntu 22.04 cannot use the release binaries.

- ELECTROBUN_MACOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET lowers the deployment target of every
  binary (Zig targets, clang -mmacosx-version-min, the CEF wrapper's
  CMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET) and the Mach-O release verifier.
- ELECTROBUN_MACOS_LAUNCHER_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET lowers only the launcher and
  the self-extractor, which use nothing newer than macOS 11.
- ELECTROBUN_LINUX_GLIBC_VERSION appends a glibc version to every Zig Linux
  target (x86_64-linux-gnu.2.35), and ELECTROBUN_LINUX_ABI_BASELINE lowers
  the limits verify-linux-elf-abi.js enforces.

Unset, every default is unchanged.
---
 package/build.ts                        | 24 ++++++---------
 package/scripts/linux-release.js        | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 package/scripts/macos-release.js        | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 package/scripts/package-release.js      |  2 +-
 package/scripts/verify-linux-elf-abi.js | 15 ++++++++--
 5 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 package/scripts/linux-release.js

